;=====================================
; The shoot tables ($2042, $2067, $2944)
;
; DIRECTION_OFFSET_TABLE ($2042) maps
; the sixteen DURL masks onto the nine
; entries of the two shoot tables, which
; is where the four "default" answers
; for two opposite arrows come from --
; LEFT and RIGHT held together is entry
; 1, no shot, and UP with both is UP.
; `s.idx` is that map with the offsets
; turned into 1-based entry numbers
; ($1F30's three `add hl,de` multiply
; the offset by three and an entry is
; six bytes, so entry = offset / 2 + 1).
