make "s.dy (list 0 -6 -6 -6 -6 -6 -6 -6 -1)

;=====================================
; The robot is the ROM's eleven bytes
; (design section 7.3)
;
; One byte wide and eleven rows tall,
; and the eleven bytes are legible as a
; drawing: 3C head, 66 eyes, FF
; shoulders, BD BD BD body, 3C hips, 24
; 24 24 legs, 66 feet. The five pattern
; tables at $1000-$1030 are the five
; facing groups -- standing, right,
; down, left, up -- and FOUR OF THEM ARE
; FOUR COSTUMES, because the fifth is
; the flip.
;
; $1155 (left) IS $112C (right)
; MIRRORED, and it is worth checking
; rather than believing: 120 is
; 01111000 and 30 is 00011110; the feet
; are 54 (00110110) against 108
; (01101100); and every other row is a
; palindrome (60, 255, 189, 36). So
; slots 10-13 are still, up, down and
; right, and `setrot "flip` walks the
; robot west in the one it already has.
; That is the second half of the saving
; that made the cabinet's twenty-one
; costumes fit in fifteen.
;
; TWELVE ROWS AND NOT ELEVEN, so every
; robot costume is one size: $1139
; (down) genuinely has twelve, its feet
; carried a row lower, and the other
; four take a blank twelfth. A uniform
; height means one erase rectangle and
; one stamp offset for all four.
